The Treasurer branch manages the financial operations of the Event Management System. It handles event budgets, expenses, revenue, payments, sponsorships, and financial records. The branch helps track transactions, monitor budget usage, manage event-related costs, and generate financial summaries, ensuring transparency, accuracy, and efficient financial management throughout the event lifecycle.
The Treasurer branch manages the financial operations of the Event Management System. It handles event budgets, expenses, revenue, payments, sponsorships, and financial records. The branch helps track transactions, monitor budget usage, manage event-related costs, and generate financial summaries, ensuring transparency, accuracy, and efficient financial management throughout the event lifecycle.

It also supports expense categorization, payment status tracking, budget allocation, sponsorship contribution records, and profit or loss calculations. The Treasurer branch works closely with the organizer, attendee, admin, and backend modules to ensure that all financial activities are properly recorded and synchronized. Its goal is to provide a reliable and organized financial structure that helps event teams make informed decisions and maintain complete control over their event finances.
